{"id": "the-solitary-woman", "ids": "⿰女⿱亠隻", "title": "The Solitary Woman", "pronunciation": "zhī", "bopomofo": "ㄓ", "meaning": "A woman who chooses solitude as a form of wisdom or spiritual cultivation", "formation": "phono-semantic", "definitions": [{"zh": "獨居修行之女子", "en": "A woman who dwells alone in spiritual practice"}, {"zh": "擇一而終之女性", "en": "A woman who chooses singular devotion to one path or principle"}, {"zh": "孤高自持之女德", "en": "The feminine virtue of maintaining dignity in solitude"}], "etymology": "In the spaces between what was written and what was felt, this character emerges from the ancient understanding that some forms of feminine wisdom require chosen isolation. The woman radical (女) embraces the phonetic element (隻), suggesting that true singularity—like that of a lone bird—can be a form of completeness rather than loss. It speaks to those women throughout history who found their strength not in companionship, but in the clarity that comes from standing apart.", "source": {"work": "《集韻》", "gloss": "⿰女⿱亠隻，之移切，女子獨修也"}, "components": [{"char": "女", "meaning": "woman"}, {"char": "亠", "meaning": "亠"}, {"char": "隻", "meaning": "隻"}], "examples": [{"text": "山中有⿰女⿱亠隻，採藥不問世事", "translation": "In the mountains there is a solitary woman who gathers herbs and asks nothing of worldly affairs", "style": "classical"}, {"text": "她選擇做一個⿰女⿱亠隻，在城市中保持內心的寧靜", "translation": "She chose to be a solitary woman, maintaining inner tranquility within the city", "style": "contemporary"}], "related": [{"char": "嫠", "pinyin": "lí", "gloss": "widow, solitary woman"}, {"char": "隻", "pinyin": "zhī", "gloss": "single, lone"}, {"char": "姝", "pinyin": "shū", "gloss": "beautiful woman"}], "tags": ["solitude", "feminine virtue", "spiritual cultivation", "classical poetry"], "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" width=\"512\" height=\"512\">\n<style>@import url(\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Serif+TC:wght@400;700&display=swap\");</st